# What the build context does NOT need.
#
# The first four lines are the whole point of this file: the target directories
# hold tens of gigabytes between them, and every one of those bytes would be
# packed, sent to the daemon and thrown away, because the image builds in a
# container that has its own empty target. A context that large also defeats the
# layer cache — any file in it changing invalidates the COPY.
target/
target-lint/
target-pkg/
target-ra/

# The git directory is history, and the build wants a working tree. Excluding it
# also keeps the branch and the remote out of the image's layers.
.git/
.githooks/

# Local agent-tooling state and host-governance files. These are gitignored for
# the same reason they are excluded here: they are not part of the product, and
# some of them name hosts and paths that have no business in a published image.
.bgv/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
MEMORY.md

# Runtime leftovers a developer's checkout accumulates. A store copied into the
# build context would be baked into a layer and shipped to everybody.
data/
*.db
*.rdb
*.log
.env
.env.*

# Editor and OS droppings.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# The image is built from the workspace, not from documentation about it.
benchmarks/
assets/
CHANGELOG.md
